Feature: Calculate Total Time Elapsed (TAT) for New Enrollment Review

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the input data is stored in the "pat_case" and "sr_activity" tables
    And the "pat_case" table has the columns "case_id", "service_request_type", and "sr_created_date"
    And the "sr_activity" table has the columns "case_id", "subject", "status", and "last_modified_date"

  Scenario Outline: Calculate TAT for New Enrollment Review
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "<start_date>"
    And the "sr_activity" table has a row with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity", "status" = "Completed", and "last_modified_date" = "<end_date>" for the corresponding "case_id"
    When the TAT is calculated
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is calculated as the difference between the end date and the start date, considering only the date value
    And the "total_time_elapsed" is adjusted for weekends
    And the result is loaded into the "tat_report" table with all columns from the "pat_case" table and the additional "total_time_elapsed" column

    Examples:
      | start_date | end_date  | total_time_elapsed |
      | 2022-01-01 | 2022-01-05 | 4                   |
      | 2022-01-01 | 2022-01-01 | 0                   |
      | 2022-01-05 | 2022-01-01 | NULL                |
      | NULL       | 2022-01-05 | NULL                |
      | 2022-01-01 | NULL       | NULL                |

  Scenario: Handle multiple "sr_activity" rows with the same "case_id" and "last_modified_date"
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "2022-01-01"
    And the "sr_activity" table has multiple rows with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity", "status" = "Completed", and "last_modified_date" = "2022-01-05" for the corresponding "case_id"
    When the TAT is calculated
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is calculated using the minimum "last_modified_date" from the "sr_activity" table

  Scenario: Handle cases where the "pat_case" table has no matching rows in the "sr_activity" table
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "2022-01-01"
    And the "sr_activity" table has no rows with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" and "status" = "Completed" for the corresponding "case_id"
    When the TAT is calculated
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is NULL

  Scenario: Validate input data format
    Given the input data is in an invalid format
    When the TAT is calculated
    Then an error is thrown with the message "Invalid input data format"

  Scenario: Validate "case_id" column as primary key
    Given the "case_id" column is not the primary key in either the "pat_case" or "sr_activity" tables
    When the TAT is calculated
    Then an error is thrown with the message "Invalid primary key"